1 0 0 1 42 428.9 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 12.5 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (Set trim and the compressor first, then EQ. The EQ is before the fader and the group outs and direct outs, so whatever you do here is) Tj T* (recorded. Reaper's ReaEQ can do the fine work later with undo; the console EQ is for broad shaping and fixing real problems.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 418.4 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (Cut before you boost. A 3 dB cut at 300 Hz does what a 3 dB boost at 3 kHz does, with less noise and less chance of clipping.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 397.4 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 12.5 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (Find a problem by sweeping: boost the mid gain, turn the FREQ knob slowly until the ugly part jumps out, then turn the gain down to a cut) Tj T* (at that spot.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 376.4 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 12.5 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (EQ moves of 1-3 dB are normal. If you need more than 6 dB, move the mic instead: an inch at the amp grille or a few inches on a vocal) Tj T* (changes more than any knob.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 344.9 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 23 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (Which mic is on the channel matters. A condenser \(Worker Bee\) has more top and more low rumble: LO CUT on, go easy on HI. Dynamic) Tj T* (mics \(SM57, SM58, the knockoffs, Peavey\) are a bit darker: small presence lifts are fine. The Turner 95D has almost no top or bottom to) Tj T* (begin with. Line sources \(synths, PV6, Tascam\) usually want no EQ at all.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 334.4 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (Stereo pairs \(rooms 5-6, Reface 12-13, SH-201 17-18, Tascam 23-24\) get identical settings, or the image shifts.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 323.9 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 2 Tm 10.5 TL /F1 8.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (\177) Tj ( ) Tj ( ) Tj (Listen in context. Solo makes everything sound like it needs more of everything. Decide with the band playing.) Tj T* ET
